proposed_comments.body:
**LOW - Log failure to create the initial settle timer**

If this first `SetTimer` call fails, the code silently removes the queued window and falls back to immediate `WindowCreated` processing. The rearm failure path already logs the Win32 error, but this initial path has no corresponding diagnostic. Please log the same error before the existing fallback so reports can identify when timer creation bypassed the settle delay. This does not change the fallback or movement behavior.

```suggestion
                    Logger::error(L"Failed to set the new window settle timer, {}", get_last_error_or_default(GetLastError()));
                    m_pendingNewWindows.Remove(hwnd);
```

